# Enforce LF line endings for all text files in the repository.
# Prevents CRLF/LF phantom diffs when working across Windows and Unix/macOS.

# Default: detect text files and normalize to LF on commit
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts — always LF (CRLF breaks shebang lines)
*.sh text eol=lf

# Source and config files — always LF
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

# Binary files — do not touch
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.tar.gz binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Before running `git add --renormalize .`, check for files whose CRLF is
# load-bearing and exempt them here with `-text` first. Some formats carry CRLF
# in the wire format itself, so normalizing them changes what the file *means*,
# not just how it is stored — parser test fixtures are the usual casualty.
# Candidates: *.ofx, *.qfx, *.qif, *.bat, *.cmd, *.ps1, *.reg, HTTP/MIME
# fixtures, and anything under a `fixtures/` or `mocks/` tree.
# `git ls-files --eol | grep 'i/crlf\|i/mixed'` lists what is currently at risk.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
